    {
      "id": "s12",
      "type": "CODE_RUN",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "In a plain script, here's how that looks. Pass a folder in when you build the context. That single argument is what switches recording on. Then your test does whatever your test does. And the file? Only turns up when you close that context. Forget the close, and you get nothing at all.",
      "data": {
        "codeRun": {
          "filename": "video.py",
          "language": "py",
          "resultLabel": "what happens",
          "color": "purple",
          "atWord": 2.583,
          "caption": "starts on create. saves on close.",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "context = browser.new_context(",
              "detail": "recording starts right here",
              "sub": "the camera is rolling",
              "label": "start",
              "atWord": 8.833
            },
            {
              "text": "    record_video_dir=\"videos/\")"
            },
            {
              "text": "page = context.new_page()"
            },
            {
              "text": "# ... your test runs ...",
              "detail": "everything gets recorded",
              "sub": "still rolling",
              "label": "live",
              "atWord": 21.417
            },
            {
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "text": "context.close()",
              "detail": "and only NOW is the file written",
              "sub": "videos/xyz.webm",
              "label": "saved",
              "atWord": 30.083
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 521,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-13-evidence_long_s12.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "type": "TERMINAL_SESSION",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "With pytest, it's a flag again, so you're never managing contexts by hand. Retain on failure records every single test, then throws the boring ones straight in the bin and keeps the failures for you.",
